  "body_html": "<h1>Behavioral Equilibrium</h1>\n<p>Let $\\Gamma$ be a finite extensive form game with perfect recall. A mixed\nequilibrium of $\\Gamma$ is a Nash equilibrium of its mixed normal-form extension.\nA behavioral equilibrium of $\\Gamma$ is a Nash equilibrium of the compact\ncontinuous game whose strategy sets are behavioral strategy spaces $B_i$ and whose\npayoffs are expected payoffs in $\\Gamma$.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Definition 6.3.5] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MechDesign.pdf</code>. Mixed and behavioral equilibria of a finite extensive game with perfect recall.</li>\n</ul>",
